# Publish guide — StarterPack-Airlock

**Zone A:** git-free working copy (develop, export, install).

**Zone B:** `{Desktop}/StarterPack-Airlock/repo/` (git, CI, human push).

## Before push

Preferred one-shot (B11):

```powershell
Verify-AirlockPublishGate.cmd
```

Or step-by-step:

1. Zone A — run tests/audit in the working copy (`run_audit.cmd` or behavior suite).
2. B09 — sync working copy into `repo/` with `pack/scripts/sync-working-copy-to-airlock-repo.ps1`.
3. Zone B — run the pack audit from `repo/` (`run_audit.cmd` from `repo/` root).
4. Human `git push` from `repo/` only — working-copy hooks refuse agent push.

`verify-audit-system.ps1 -PublishRoot .../StarterPack-Airlock/repo` runs an optional Zone B behavior pass after the working-copy pass.

## First-time layout

**Recommended:** parallel build — working copy keeps git until publish is proven:

```powershell
Initialize-StarterPackAirlock.cmd -GitMode Copy
Verify-AirlockPublishGate.cmd
# ... remote, push, CI ...
Complete-StarterPackAirlockCutover.cmd
```

Full checklist: `docs/AIRLOCK_MIGRATION_CHECKLIST.md` in the working copy.

**Human-only:** agent hooks refuse `git push` from the working copy (H01). Push from `repo/` only.
